Compose a memorial of thanks from the assembled officials upon receiving imperially bestowed copies of Selected Essentials of Medical Prescriptions (Yifang xuanyao).
Legal judgments 〔five items〕:
An official exceeding the time limit for reporting to his post;
Eating melons or fruit from fields or gardens without permission;
Illicitly passing checkpoints or crossing ferries under false pretenses;
Military personnel and commoners arranging jointly to bring lawsuits;
Repairing bridges and roads.
Third Session
Five Policy Questions
Question: From antiquity, emperors and kings achieved harmonious and flourishing government through learning that continually advanced toward illumination. All took reverent attentiveness as essential to establishing the supreme standard. The ages of Tang Yao and Yu Shun and the Three Dynasties cannot be surpassed. By the Han, Tang, and Song dynasties, however, the method of cultivating the mind was no longer transmitted; government attained only modest order and offers nothing worth discussing. Our Emperor Taizu Gao founded the realm and established its supreme standard, tracing the transmission of the method of cultivating the mind back to the sages of old. He once commanded his Confucian officials to write out the Great Plan (Hongfan) and display it beside his seat. He read it morning and evening, and himself undertook to …
